The CEDFrequencyMerger and CEDTemporalMapper definitions and initialization
are retained from Mizar runtime/stage1/models/ced.py. The CED encoder model
code and weights are separate remote assets and retain their own terms.

This isolated route loads all original final-checkpoint states, shares
layers 19-22 across four passes without added injection, and trains only
those four layers. It uses online CED audio decoding/staging, explicit
training audits, eight-GPU microbatch-four with four-step gradient
accumulation, and complete-state checkpoints. The recipe is adapted from
the current mizar_l9_12x3_strong_reason AudioMCQ training route.
